hadiths[28]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16456","al-Hajjaj ibn Muhammad and Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, they said: Layth, meaning Ibn Sa'd, narrated to us, he said: Bukayr, meaning Ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, narrated to me, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Zayd ibn Khalid, from Abu Talha, companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The angels do not enter a house in which there is an image. Busr said: Then he fell ill and we visited him, and on his door was a curtain with an image. So I said to Ubayd Allah al-Khawlani, the foster son of Maymuna, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Did he not inform us and mention images on the first day. So Ubayd Allah said: Did you not hear him say: Except a figure on a garment. Hashim said: Did Zayd not inform us about images on the first day. So Ubayd Allah said: Did you not hear him when he said: Except a figure on a garment. And so said Yunus."
"16457","Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, and Ibn Abi Za'ida said: Hajjaj informed us, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Talha informed me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, combined between Hajj and Umra."
"16458","And Abd al-Razzaq said: Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas say: I heard Abu Talha say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog nor an image of statues."
"16459","Rawh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, from Abu Talha, he said: When the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, attacked Khaybar in the morning, and they had taken their spades and gone out early to their fields and lands, then when they saw the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with the army, they ran back retreating. So the Prophet of Allah said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest. When we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of the warned."
"16460","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: It was said to Matar al-Warraq while I was with him: From whom did al-Hasan take that he performs ablution from what fire has altered. He said: He took it from Anas, and Anas took it from Abu Talha, and Abu Talha took it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"16461","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Hafs narrated to us, from al-Agharr, from another man, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Perform ablution from what fire has altered."
"16462","And Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Hafs, said: He said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Talha, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"16463","Then he said: And Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"16464","Husayn narrated to us, in the tafsir of Shayban, from Qatada, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated that Abu Talha said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, attacked Khaybar in the morning, and they had taken their spades and gone out early to their fields. Then when they saw the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with the army, they turned back retreating. So the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest. Khaybar is ruined. When we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of the warned. He said:"
"16465","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Qatada, His saying, Exalted and Majestic: Then when it descends in their courtyard, evil is the morning of the warned. He said: Anas ibn Malik narrated from Abu Talha, he said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, attacked Khaybar in the morning, and he mentioned the like of it."
"16466","Surayj narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn Ujra, from Abu Talha al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, woke one day cheerful, with brightness seen in his face. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you woke today cheerful, with brightness seen in your face. He said: Yes, a comer from my Lord, Exalted and Majestic, came to me and said: Whoever of your umma sends one blessing upon you, Allah writes for him ten good deeds, and erases from him ten evil deeds, and raises for him ten degrees, and returns to him the like of it."
"16467","Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Talha, raising it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The angels do not enter a house in which there is an image nor a dog."
"16468","Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'ida narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj informed us, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Talha informed me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, combined between a Hajj and an Umra."
"16469","Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, from Abu Talha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he overcame a people, liked to stay in their courtyard three."
"16470","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, he said: Sa'id informed us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, from Abu Talha, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he fought a people and defeated them, stayed in the courtyard three. And on the day of Badr he ordered the chiefs of Quraysh and they were thrown in a foul stinking well of the wells of Badr. He said: Then he went to them, and we went with him, then said: O Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, and O Utba ibn Rabi'a, and O Shayba ibn Rabi'a, and O Walid ibn Utba, have you found what your Lord promised you true, for I have found what my Lord promised me true. He said: So Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, do you speak to bodies with no souls in them. He said: By Him Who sent me with the truth, you are not more hearing of what I say than them. Qatada said: Allah sent them to hear His speech as rebuke and abasement and humiliation. He said at the beginning of the hadith: When he finished with the people of Badr, he stayed in the courtyard three."
"16471","Yunus narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, and Husayn in the tafsir of Shayban, from Qatada, he said: And Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that Abu Talha said: Drowsiness overcame us while we were in our ranks on the day of Badr. Abu Talha said: And I was among those overcome by drowsiness that day, so my sword kept falling from my hand and I would take it, and it would fall and I would take it."
"16472","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, from Abu Talha, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, attacked Khaybar in the morning, and they had taken their spades and gone out early to their fields and lands, then when they saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with the army, they turned back retreating. So the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest. When we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of the warned."
"16473","Rawh narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatada, he said: Anas ibn Malik mentioned to us, from Abu Talha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered on the day of Badr with twenty-four men of the chiefs of Quraysh, and they were thrown in a foul tainted well of the wells of Badr. And when he prevailed over a people, he stayed in the courtyard three nights. Then when at Badr on the third day, he ordered his mount and its saddle was tied upon it, then he walked and his companions followed him. So he said: We thought only that he was going to relieve himself, until he stood on the edge of the well and called them by their names and the names of their fathers: O so-and-so son of so-and-so, and O so-and-so son of so-and-so, would it please you that you obeyed Allah and His Messenger. We have found what our Lord promised us true, so have you found what your Lord promised true. So Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, why do you speak to bodies with no souls in them. So he said: By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are not more hearing of what I say than them. Qatada said: Allah gave them life until He made them hear His speech as rebuke and belittling and humiliation and regret and remorse. He said:"
"16474","Husayn narrated to us, from Shayban, and he did not trace it to its source, from Abu Talha, he said: And humiliation."
"16475","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, he said: Sulayman, freedman of al-Hasan ibn Ali, came to us in the time of al-Hajjaj and narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Talha, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came one day with brightness seen in his face. So we said: We see brightness in your face. So he said: An angel came to me and said: O Muhammad, your Lord says: Does it not please you that none of your umma sends blessing upon you except I send ten upon him, and none sends peace upon you except I send peace ten upon him."
"16476","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Ibn Shihab, from Ibn Abi Talha, from Abu Talha, he said: Shu'ba said: And I think he mentioned it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Perform ablution from what fire has cooked."
"16477","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Sulayman, freedman of al-Hasan ibn Ali, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Talha, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came one day with joy seen in his face. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, we see joy in your face. So he said: An angel came to me and said: O Muhammad, does it not please you that your Lord, Exalted and Majestic, says: None of your umma sends blessing upon you except I send ten upon him, and none of your umma sends peace upon you except I send peace ten upon him. He said: Yes indeed."
"16478","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, he said: Sulayman, freedman of al-Hasan ibn Ali, came to us in the time of al-Hajjaj and narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Talha, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came one day with brightness seen in his face, and he mentioned it."
"16479","Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqba narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Uqba, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I and Ubayy ibn Ka'b and Abu Talha were sitting, and we ate meat and bread. Then I called for ablution, so they said: Why do you perform ablution. I said: For this food we ate. So they said: Do you perform ablution from good things. One better than you did not perform ablution."
"16480","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harb ibn Thabit, who lived among Banu Sulaym, narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talha narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: A man recited before Umar and he corrected him. So he said: I recited to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he did not correct me. He said: So we gathered at the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So the man recited to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said to him: You did well. He said: As if Umar felt something from that. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Umar, the Quran is all correct, so long as punishment is not made forgiveness or forgiveness punishment. And Abd al-Samad said another time: Abu Thabit, from his book."
"16481","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talha narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Abu Talha said: We were sitting in the courtyards, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by us and said: What is with you and sittings on the roads. Avoid sittings on the roads. He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, we sat without harm, remembering and conversing. He said: Then give the sittings their due. We said: And what is their due. He said: Lowering the gaze, returning the greeting, and good speech."
"16482","Ahmad ibn Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us, he said: Layth ibn Sa'd informed us, and he mentioned a hadith. He said: And Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to me, he said: Yahya ibn Sulaym ibn Zayd, freedman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to me that he heard Isma'il ibn Bashir, freedman of Banu Mughala, say: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah and Abu Talha ibn Sahl, the two Ansaris, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No man forsakes a Muslim man at a place where his sanctity is violated and his honor is diminished, except Allah, Exalted and Majestic, will forsake him at a place where he loves His help. And no man helps a Muslim man at a place where his honor is diminished and his sanctity is violated, except Allah will help him at a place where he loves His help."
"16483","Affan narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us, he said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih informed us, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Abu Talha al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog nor an image."
